[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The task renders the whole canon by default, writes both wrappers, and a second task serves the page on loopback

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-VIEW-SERVE
TITLE: The task renders the whole canon by default, writes both wrappers, and a second task serves the page on loopback
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
view:render with no root renders every root into output/view/canon.html
(a full page: doctype, head with title and viewport, body) and
output/view/canon.artifact.html (the same content in the artifact host's
shape); with --input root=UID it renders one root as the same page with one
root. view:serve serves output/view on 127.0.0.1 and prints the address. The
page is self-contained -- no fetch, fonts with fallbacks, the payload
inlined -- so the file opens from disk without the server.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-VIEW-SERVES-LOCALLY-AND-AS-AN-ARTIFACT
  ROLE: Governed_By
